From 7e13ec44cd3f504eec4406a47a29ea4a7649d4f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Dev Auditor <audit@massbattle.local>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:56:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] phase2-audit: delete the dead DrainCompositePool seam
 (A-3)

FMeleeMath::DrainCompositePool was never called by any runtime path: the
resolution processor implements the mount-first drain INLINE (integer-hit
model: DefenderMountRemaining-- then the existing FDeadTag path when the
rider is exposed), which is the path T2.6/ChargeMechanics verified
end-to-end. The seam's float-damage signature (RiderHP, Damage) never
matched the shipped integer-hit model -- so wiring it in would have been
a behavior change, not a refactor. A tested function no runtime uses is
a trap for the next maintainer (it looks like the place to change
combat drain; it isn't).

Deleted: the seam function, its header declaration, its golden block in
FHitChanceGolden (the assertion set was duplicated coverage of dead code
-- the real drain behavior is covered by ChargeMechanics), and the stale
composite-HP constant comment. A replacement comment in the golden test
records where the real drain lives.

MUST re-run the unit tier on the UE machine (T2.1 golden shrinks by one
block; expected green).
